# The repo carries the mod and its documentation. Everything else here is a
# local working set: game jars, the mod corpus, test servers, generated
# analysis. All of it is either huge, re-derivable from the engine, or someone
# else's copyrighted code.

# --- game + corpus data (never distributable) ---
data/

# --- build output ---
build/
out/
core/build/
core/out-*/
*.class
*.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# --- generated analysis, re-derivable via stub-diff / class-fate / convert ---
core/out-diff/
core/audit-*.md

# --- segment diffs: regenerated from the stubs by gen-segment, not build input ---
core/segments/*__*.json

# --- kill-list tooling: drives the closure workflow, never ships in the jar ---
core/tools/

# --- working notes, not documentation ---
LOOP.md

# --- research scaffolding, superseded by the Java engine ---
analyzer/
cb/

# --- runtime scratch ---
run/
logs/
crash-reports/
*.log
.gradle/
.idea/
*.iml
__pycache__/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
